title: 'linearly: the math of AI, drawn and coded'
authors:
  - family-names: Khalilli
    given-names: Ali
  - name: 'The linearly contributors'
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-01'
abstract: >-
  A free linear algebra course for people building AI, taught picture first:
  every lecture pairs a plain-language article with hand-drawn diagrams,
  interactive components, and the same worked examples in NumPy, PyTorch, JAX,
  and TensorFlow. A reading companion to MIT 18.06.
